### Solana Hackathon Winners Raise Over $700M, New Accelerator Launched

**GLOBAL** – Winning teams from Solana ecosystem hackathons have raised over $700 million in venture capital in the past four years, cementing the events as a key launchpad for new technology companies. Building on this success, a new accelerator program has been established by the organization Colosseum to provide $250,000 in pre-seed funding to future winners.

The hackathons have attracted more than 80,000 participants from around the world, resulting in the creation of thousands of new products on the Solana network. These events draw significant support from major technology and finance companies, with past sponsors including Google Cloud, Microsoft, Stripe, Coinbase, and Amazon Web Services. Their involvement aims to provide developers with the resources needed for innovation.

The new accelerator by Colosseum formalizes a pathway from competition to company. All hackathon winners will now be considered for the program. Accepted teams receive the $250,000 investment to kickstart their ventures.

Colosseum, which collaborates with top founders, developers, and investors for judging and mentorship, will also provide the selected startups with exclusive access to an elite founder network and direct 1:1 mentorship. The initiative is designed to streamline the journey for promising projects emerging from the competitive hackathon environment.

