**T-Systems Launches AI-Powered Service to Speed Up Corporate Cloud Transitions**

**BONN, Germany** – T-Systems, the IT services subsidiary of Deutsche Telekom, announced on Thursday the launch of "T-Systems @Vantage," a new artificial intelligence-based service designed to accelerate companies' migration to the cloud.

The offering provides an end-to-end solution for businesses looking to modernize their legacy IT infrastructure. T-Systems @Vantage is a modular package that includes advisory services, cloud migration, application modernization, and managed services. The integration of AI aims to make the transformation process faster and more effective by automating complex tasks.

According to the company, the AI component analyzes application architecture, translates programming languages, documents processes, and conducts autonomous testing. This approach is intended to tackle complex legacy systems that were previously considered too difficult or expensive to update, with T-Systems claiming customers could see cost savings of up to 30% and release changes up to 15 times faster. The service is also designed to be a sovereign and secure offering, utilizing T-Systems' European cloud platforms to ensure compliance with local regulations.

"Many customers have started their transformation to the cloud, but the expected results have not materialized," said Ferri Abolhassan, CEO of T-Systems. "Cloud computing is only successful when applications are modernized, not simply lifted and shifted to the cloud." Abolhassan noted that the new service addresses common challenges, such as unexpected complexity and a failure to achieve expected efficiency gains during IT transformations.

