**Daimler Truck, HHLA, and Kawasaki Partner to Build European Liquid Hydrogen Supply Chain**

**HAMBURG, Germany** – Daimler Truck AG, Hamburger Hafen und Logistik AG (HHLA), and Kawasaki Heavy Industries have launched a strategic partnership to establish a liquid hydrogen supply chain for Europe. The three companies signed a Memorandum of Understanding on October 22 at the Hydrogen Technology World Expo in Hamburg.

The collaboration aims to develop a reliable and cost-effective system for importing green liquid hydrogen through the Port of Hamburg and distributing it to the European hinterland. The partners will assess the logistical requirements for transshipment and transportation via road and rail in the coming months.

This initiative seeks to position Hamburg as a central hub for sustainable energy imports and accelerate the decarbonization of transport and industry. The partners bring distinct expertise to the project: Kawasaki as a technology provider for hydrogen infrastructure, HHLA as a European logistics and port operator, and Daimler Truck as a manufacturer of hydrogen-powered commercial vehicles, including its Mercedes-Benz GenH2 Truck.

The project also intends to attract additional companies to form a consortium covering the entire hydrogen value chain, from production to end-use, reinforcing the push for a hydrogen-based economy in Europe.

